### Fix 1 — Discord role sync on admin Activate / Cancel

**File:** `src/app/api/admin/members/[id]/route.ts`

When an admin activates or cancels a member, the DB is updated but the Discord role is not assigned or removed.

The Discord role helper functions already exist in other routes and follow this pattern:

**Assign role:**
```ts
async function assignDiscordRole(discordId: string): Promise<void> {
  const botToken = process.env.DISCORD_BOT_TOKEN;
  const guildId = process.env.DISCORD_GUILD_ID;
  const roleId = process.env.DISCORD_ROLE_ID;
  if (!botToken || !guildId || !roleId || !discordId) return;

  const res = await fetch(
    `https://discord.com/api/v10/guilds/${guildId}/members/${discordId}/roles/${roleId}`,
    {
      method: "PUT",
      headers: {
        Authorization: `Bot ${botToken}`,
        "Content-Length": "0",
      },
    }
  );

  if (!res.ok && res.status !== 204) {
    const body = await res.text();
    console.error("[Admin] Failed to assign Discord role:", res.status, body);
  } else {
    console.log(`[Admin] Assigned Discord role to ${discordId}`);
  }
}
```

**Remove role:**
```ts
async function removeDiscordRole(discordId: string): Promise<void> {
  const botToken = process.env.DISCORD_BOT_TOKEN;
  const guildId = process.env.DISCORD_GUILD_ID;
  const roleId = process.env.DISCORD_ROLE_ID;
  if (!botToken || !guildId || !roleId || !discordId) return;

  const res = await fetch(
    `https://discord.com/api/v10/guilds/${guildId}/members/${discordId}/roles/${roleId}`,
    {
      method: "DELETE",
      headers: { Authorization: `Bot ${botToken}` },
    }
  );

  if (!res.ok && res.status !== 204) {
    const body = await res.text();
    console.error("[Admin] Failed to remove Discord role:", res.status, body);
  } else {
    console.log(`[Admin] Removed Discord role from ${discordId}`);
  }
}
```

**Changes needed in the `activate` action:**
1. After updating the user/subscription in DB, fetch the user's `discord_id`:
   ```ts
   const userRow = await sql`SELECT discord_id FROM users WHERE id = ${userId}`;
   const discordId = userRow[0]?.discord_id as string | null;
   if (discordId) await assignDiscordRole(discordId);
   ```

**Changes needed in the `cancel` action:**
1. After updating the user/subscription in DB, fetch the user's `discord_id` and call `removeDiscordRole`:
   ```ts
   const userRow = await sql`SELECT discord_id FROM users WHERE id = ${userId}`;
   const discordId = userRow[0]?.discord_id as string | null;
   if (discordId) await removeDiscordRole(discordId);
   ```

Also apply the same Discord role removal to the `expire` action, since expiring a member should also strip their Discord access (this is consistent with what the cron job does).

---

### Fix 2 — Remove the test-db route

**File:** `src/app/api/test-db/route.ts`

This file exposes raw database contents with no authentication. It must be deleted (replaced with a 404 response or simply removed from the repo).

Replace the file content with a simple 404 response so it doesn't expose data:

```ts
import { NextResponse } from "next/server";

export async function GET() {
  return NextResponse.json({ error: "Not found" }, { status: 404 });
}
```

---

### Fix 3 — Fix MRR calculation in AdminPanel

**File:** `src/app/dashboard/AdminPanel.tsx`

Currently the MRR is calculated from the `members` state array in the browser, which gets filtered by the search input. This means when a search is active, the MRR shows an incorrect number based only on the filtered results.

**The fix:** Separate the MRR calculation so it always uses the **full unfiltered member list**. 

The `fetchMembers` function currently replaces the entire `members` array with the search result. Instead:

1. Add a second state variable `allMembers` that is only set on the initial load (empty search):
   ```ts
   const [allMembers, setAllMembers] = useState<Member[]>([]);
   ```

2. In `fetchMembers`, when `q` is empty, update both `members` and `allMembers`. When `q` is non-empty, only update `members`:
   ```ts
   const fetchMembers = useCallback(async (q: string) => {
     setLoading(true);
     try {
       const url = q
         ? `/api/admin/members?search=${encodeURIComponent(q)}`
         : "/api/admin/members";
       const res = await fetch(url);
       if (res.ok) {
         const data = await res.json();
         setMembers(data);
         if (!q) setAllMembers(data);
       }
     } finally {
       setLoading(false);
     }
   }, []);
   ```

