Fixes #224

## Root cause

\shouldShowEmptyOverlay()\ returned \	rue\ unconditionally when \hasConfiguredDrawPiles\ was false — even when pinned (ungrouped) context cards were present. The overlay covered the entire page, hiding the Pinned cards section.

## Fix

Gate the overlay on \hasVisibleContext\ first:

\\\	s
// Before
return !homeState.summary.hasConfiguredDrawPiles || (
  !homeState.summary.hasVisibleContext &&
  homeState.summary.remainingDrawCount === 0
);

// After
return !homeState.summary.hasVisibleContext && (
  !homeState.summary.hasConfiguredDrawPiles || homeState.summary.remainingDrawCount === 0
);
\\\

The overlay now only appears when there is genuinely nothing to show.

## What
Promotes `scheduleContext` from a read-only facade into a `protocolSession` module that owns **both** reads and writes for the protocol seam.

## Why
Three routes bypassed the store by instantiating Dexie adapters inline:
- `+page.svelte` — new'd `DexieQuestionnaireRepository` + `DexieScheduleRepository` to run `startProtocol`
- `program/+page.svelte` — new'd `DexieScheduleRepository` to persist `appendReTestPhases` / `removeReTestPhase`
- `settings/+page.svelte` — called `db.answers.clear() / db.schedule.clear()` directly

`protocolSession` collapses these three doors into one named API. Routes no longer import `$lib/db/atopic-db` or any adapter class. `subscribe` delegates to `scheduleContext` so the 6 read-only routes are unaffected.

## Examples

Before:
```ts
import { db } from '$lib/db/atopic-db';
import { DexieQuestionnaireRepository } from '$lib/adapters/dexie-questionnaire-repository';
import { DexieScheduleRepository } from '$lib/adapters/dexie-schedule-repository';
const questionnaireRepo = new DexieQuestionnaireRepository(db);
const scheduleRepo = new DexieScheduleRepository(db);
const schedule = generateSchedule(answers);
await questionnaireRepo.save(answers);
await scheduleRepo.save(schedule);
```

After:
```ts
import { protocolSession } from '$lib/stores/protocol-session';
await protocolSession.startProtocol(answers);
```

