After the theme migration, the homepage was rendering as plain text/navigation with no visual hero treatment, so the “On Air” banner effect and overlaid messaging were lost. This PR restores a branded, high-contrast banner while keeping the site on Blowfish and respecting the existing `homepage.layout = "custom"` configuration.

- **Homepage layout implementation (`custom`)**
  - Added `/src/layouts/partials/home/custom.html` so Blowfish can resolve and render the configured custom homepage layout instead of falling back to default profile/page behavior.
  - Uses homepage content front matter (`headline`) and page body as the hero copy source.

- **Banner image restoration**
  - Reads banner image from `homepage.homepageImage` (with fallback to `defaultBackgroundImage`).
  - Supports remote URLs and local paths via Hugo resources / site-relative URL resolution.

- **UX and accessibility improvements in hero treatment**
  - Reintroduces full-width hero image with readable overlayed text.
  - Applies stronger overlay contrast and text shadows for consistent legibility.
  - Adds semantic region labeling and hides decorative overlay from assistive tech.
  - Includes a no-image fallback section that still renders structured heading/content.

```go-html-template
{{ $heroImageURL := "" }}
{{ with .Site.Params.homepage.homepageImage | default .Site.Params.defaultBackgroundImage }}
  {{ if or (strings.HasPrefix . "http://") (strings.HasPrefix . "https://") }}
    {{ $heroImageURL = . }}
  {{ else }}
    {{ with resources.Get . }}
      {{ $heroImageURL = .RelPermalink }}
    {{ else }}
      {{ $heroImageURL = . | relURL }}
    {{ end }}
  {{ end }}
{{ end }}
```

